Subject: WebKit: fix NetworkCache::Data construction from an 8-bit source span

ENABLE_CONTENT_EXTENSIONS was off on the PlayStation port partly because
APIContentRuleListStore.cpp does not compile: Data(sourceJSON.span8())
is an ambiguous functional-style cast from std::span<const Latin1Character>
(Latin1Character is not uint8_t on this toolchain) between the
Vector<uint8_t>&& and the CURL Variant<...> constructors. The intended
constructor is Data(std::span<const uint8_t>); reinterpret the 8-bit span to
bytes with asBytes(), exactly as the sibling 16-bit branch already does.
Needed for ENABLE_CONTENT_EXTENSIONS on the PS5 build (the ad blocker's
WKContentRuleList).

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/APIContentRuleListStore.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/APIContentRuleListStore.cpp
index 061e4605a..2a9698bec 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/APIContentRuleListStore.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/APIContentRuleListStore.cpp
@@ -339,7 +339,7 @@ static std::expected<MappedData, std::error_code> compiledToFile(WTF::String&& j
             writeToFile(sourceJSON.is8Bit());
             m_sourceWritten += sizeof(bool);
             if (sourceJSON.is8Bit()) {
-                writeToFile(WebKit::NetworkCache::Data(sourceJSON.span8()));
+                writeToFile(WebKit::NetworkCache::Data(asBytes(sourceJSON.span8())));
                 m_sourceWritten += sourceJSON.length();
             } else {
                 writeToFile(WebKit::NetworkCache::Data(asBytes(sourceJSON.span16())));
